<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cleartext HTTP is permitted process-wide, ON PURPOSE, for this PoC.

  Why not a scoped rule: Android's network security config has no CIDR
  support. `<domain>` entries are matched as hostname strings (an IP literal
  matches exactly, `includeSubdomains` is DNS-label semantics), so a rule such
  as `<domain>100.64.0.0</domain>` permits cleartext for that ONE literal host
  and denies every real tailnet address (100.x.y.z). The earlier version of this
  file claimed to scope the CGNAT range and did not (caught in review).

  Why cleartext at all: the gateway is reached over the tailnet, where the
  transport is already encrypted by WireGuard. A self-hosted Hermes gateway
  serves plain HTTP on its tailnet address; requiring https:// would break the
  intended pairing flow (the core validates the scheme of the payload and
  accepts http/https).

  Consequence, stated plainly: any http:// host is reachable from this app in
  a build with this file. That is acceptable for the PoC and must be revisited
  before any release (either an https reverse proxy in front of the gateway,
  or a runtime allowlist of the paired host in the app's own HTTP layer).
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
